# Programs network edge cases

Use `page.route` only to force the programs response whose **UI reaction** is the subject of that test. Fulfill `/api/programs` (list `GET`, create `POST`) or `/api/programs/:id` (`PATCH` save). `route.continue()` every other method. Never fulfill `/api/auth/*`.

Never mock the call the test is actually verifying. A test that checks a real create, update, or list does not fulfill that request. Do not assert the status code you fulfilled. `page.unroute` before a later step that must hit the real API (empty-list setup, then a real create).

Register the route before the action that sends the request. UI actions go through `ProgramsPage`, `NewProgramModal`, and `LoginPage` only. `page.route` / `page.unroute` stay in the spec. Success helpers wait for **201** or a closed dialog (`createProgram`, `submitCreate`) — do not use them for a non-success fulfillment. Use `attemptCreate` or `clickCreate(track, { required: false })` for a failed create, and `clickSave` for a failed update. If `goto()` waits for a table or empty state the error screen never shows, propose a POM change; do not replace it with raw locators or `page.goto`.

One Playwright suite tag per test (see `playwright-conventions.mdc` §11): use `@regression` for network edge cases unless the scenario is a short critical path (`@smoke` / `@sanity`). Not an array. Name tests so `-g "programs-save-503"` can filter a single status.

Before any assertion, open the real programs page (Playwright MCP → `agent-browser` → Playwright CLI) and read the error and empty-state copy the app renders. Assert that text. If a case renders nothing, say so and assert the shell stayed up (no crash, programs URL still loaded). Do not invent strings. Do not reuse another status's copy.

Each row is its own test. List body the app expects is JSON `{ "data": [ ... ] }`. Empty list fulfills **200** `{ "data": [] }`.

| Call | Fulfill | Assert |
|---|---|---|
| Save (`POST` or `PATCH`) | **503** | UI error state, live copy |
| Save | **401, 403, 404, 501, 502, 400, 409, 422, 429, 500, 504, 408** | UI error state, or the live redirect; copy from the page |
| Save | **300** | App does not crash; record the rendered copy or "renders nothing" |
| `GET` list | **200** `{ "data": [] }` | Empty-state message, live copy |
| `GET` list | **200** non-JSON body | App does not crash |
| `GET` list | **200** JSON whose `data` is not an array (`{ "data": {} }`) | App does not crash |
| `GET` list | **401, 403, 404, 501, 502, 503, 300, 204, 400, 500, 504, 408** | What the page actually shows (error, redirect, empty, or nothing). A failed list must not be asserted as the empty state unless recon showed that |

```typescript
test('programs-save-503 surfaces the unavailable error', { tag: '@regression' }, async ({ page, trackProgram }) => {
  const programsPage = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programsPage.goto();
  await programsPage.openNewProgramForm();
  await programsPage.modal.fill(name, description);
  await page.route(/\/api\/programs$/, async (route) => {
    if (route.request().method() !== 'POST') {
      await route.continue();
      return;
    }
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 503,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({ message: 'Service Unavailable' }),
    });
  });
  await programsPage.modal.clickCreate(trackProgram, { required: false });
  // Assert the error string read from the live page. If it rendered nothing, say so.
});
```
